# Everything the build does not need. Keeping this tight matters twice over:
# a smaller context uploads faster, and node_modules from the host would
# shadow the ones the image installs for its own platform.
**/node_modules
# infra/ stages this whole directory as a Lambda image asset, and the staging
# output lands in infra/cdk.out — inside the directory being staged. Without
# these, each asset copies the previous one's output into itself and `cdk synth`
# dies with ENAMETOOLONG after nesting the path forty-odd times.
#
# Both lines are needed: one for the directory, one for what is under it. The
# stack repeats the same exclusion on the asset itself, because CDK reads this
# file first and the last matching pattern wins — the `.env.example` re-include
# below would otherwise pull those files back out of a directory excluded here.
cdk.out
**/cdk.out/**
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
.git
.github
.claude
.idea
.vscode
designs
docs
web
*.md
!README.md
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/logs
.gh-token
